          "start": 437.01,
          "end": 439.14,
          "en": "when you are using the image component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 439.14,
          "end": 442.14,
          "en": "as we did it in the header on an image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 442.14,
          "end": 445.14,
          "en": "that's imported from the local filesystem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 445.14,
          "end": 447.66,
          "en": "as we're doing it here with the logo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 447.66,
          "end": 448.5,
          "en": "In that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 448.5,
          "end": 451.89300000000003,
          "en": "NextJS is able to look up the width and height.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 453.03,
          "end": 454.89,
          "en": "But for those meal items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 454.89,
          "end": 458.31,
          "en": "we'll load them dynamically from a database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 458.31,
          "end": 459.78,
          "en": "And then in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 459.78,
          "end": 462.57,
          "en": "we'll have a path pointing to some image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 462.57,
          "end": 465.39,
          "en": "and NextJS will not be able to resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 465.39,
          "end": 467.55,
          "en": "the width and height of such an image,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 467.55,
          "end": 470.86,
          "en": "of such a dynamically loaded and resolved image",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 472.35,
          "end": 474.09000000000003,
          "en": "simply because the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 474.09000000000003,
          "end": 476.4,
          "en": "is not available at build time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 476.4,
          "end": 479.13,
          "en": "as it's the case for all imported images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 479.13,
          "end": 480.753,
          "en": "but only at runtime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 481.68,
          "end": 485.163,
          "en": "And that's why I added this special fill prop here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 486,
          "end": 488.97,
          "en": "An alternative would've been to explicitly set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 488.97,
          "end": 492.51,
          "en": "the width and height of the images that will be output here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 492.51,
          "end": 495.42,
          "en": "but the problem is that I don't know that in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 495.42,
          "end": 497.1,
          "en": "because we'll also be dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 497.1,
          "end": 499.203,
          "en": "with images shared by the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 500.19,
          "end": 504.45,
          "en": "And in such scenarios, fill is an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 504.45,
          "end": 506.49,
          "en": "This then tells NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 506.49,
          "end": 509.25,
          "en": "that it should simply fill the available space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 509.25,
          "end": 513.75,
          "en": "with that image as defined by its parent components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 513.75,
          "end": 516.84,
          "en": "And I set up appropriate CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 516.84,
          "end": 519.153,
          "en": "that make sure that this will look good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 520.29,
          "end": 521.64,
          "en": "And I'm mentioning this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 521.64,
          "end": 524.07,
          "en": "because it is of course a common scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 524.07,
          "end": 526.5,
          "en": "that you're displaying images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 526.5,
          "end": 530.49,
          "en": "where you might not know their dimensions in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 530.49,
          "end": 534.51,
          "en": "And in such cases, fill is a great alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 534.51,
          "end": 537.72,
          "en": "to explicitly setting a width or height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 537.72,
          "end": 539.61,
          "en": "which you should do though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 539.61,
          "end": 542.673,
          "en": "if you know the width and height in advance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 544.44,
          "end": 547.26,
          "en": "So that's therefore this MealItem component added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 547.26,
          "end": 548.55,
          "en": "And with that added,",
